{"id": "1544910294180958208", "channel_id": "1544910294180958208", "author_id": "1430896214068564059", "author_name": "ssandcc1314", "content": "为什么不能在每次出牌前看到这张卡牌未来可能造成的伤害？你毕竟是一个卡牌游戏，伤害总要靠玩家自己猜，有什么意义？卡牌游戏的快乐不就是合理的分配资源用恰到好处的伤害杀死怪物吗？我不想再赌“我能杀了它”，结果就差一点点伤害需要重开了！\n\"Why can't I see the potential damage this card will deal before I actually play it? After all, this is a card game—why should players have to guess the damage output? What's the point? Isn't the fun of card games about wisely allocating resources and dealing just the right amount of damage to finish off a monster? I don't want to keep gambling on 'I can kill it,' only to miss by a tiny bit of damage and have to restart the whole fight!\"", "timestamp": "2026-09-03T03:21:57.178000+00:00", "thread_id": "1544910294180958208", "thread_title": "需要伤害预览", "forum_channel_id": "1180845276823564288", "thread_tags": ["1542484945447026708", "1542484013652910141"], "is_thread_starter": true}
{"id": "1544893833400029184", "channel_id": "1544396502162608228", "author_id": "422766128826417152", "author_name": "blackdonut5182", "content": "------------ The text below might be somewhat unpleasant to read.----------\n\nI am spending money on this game because I really love it. I like the story, but the content is lacking and translation errors are constant.\n\nEspecially considering the nature of the game genre and the importance of the story, translation issues are unacceptable.\n\nA vicious cycle of the situation improving only to worsen again keeps repeating.\n\nIn this situation, the fact that I have to spend more money just to properly enjoy the game makes me question whether it is truly worth investing so much money in this game.\n\nTo be honest, I have been spending money hoping the company wouldn't go bankrupt because I liked the game's atmosphere, story, OST, illustrations, and concept so much.\n\nHowever, having to spend money because of game balance issues is a completely different matter.\n\nTo be frank, I only spend about $80 to $100 a month, or at most $300, but if I had used that money to play other blockbuster games, I could have enjoyed them much more.\n\nIn other games, you can enjoy them without any problems just by pulling characters or weapons.\n\nThat is because the difficulty is set to that level in the first place.\n\nAlso, people sometimes invest more because doing so allows them to enjoy the content more easily and comfortably, or perhaps because they have an affection for the characters.\n\nIf the goal is to induce spending by increasing the game's difficulty,\n\nI believe that rich and high-quality content should be provided to match.\n\nI sincerely hope that this game succeeds and the company grows further so that we can enjoy the game with better quality and translation in the future.\n\n<:Horla_cry:1357186646294138890>", "timestamp": "2026-09-03T02:16:32.622000+00:00", "thread_id": "1544396502162608228", "edited_timestamp": "2026-09-03T02:16:55.399000+00:00", "reactions": [{"emoji": "❤️", "emoji_id": null, "count": 3}], "thread_title": "I can't understand the developer's way of thinking.", "forum_channel_id": "1180845276823564288", "thread_tags": ["1542484945447026708", "1542479601241030726"]}
{"id": "1544865965387546634", "channel_id": "1544152565921611837", "author_id": "344158840448745472", "author_name": "bang8509", "content": "Do you genuinely think this is a reasonable level of difficulty, and that’s why you decided to rework D-tide this way?\n\nHonestly, if you had just kept the previous difficulty, I think far fewer people would be complaining about it right now.\n\nI’m extremely disappointed that this is what I get after putting so much love, time, and money into Morimens. I’ve spent over $4,000 on this game, and I’ve attached screenshots of my decks to show just how much I’ve invested into the game.\n\nBut from now on, I’m done spending money, and I’m going to stop doing D-tide altogether.\n\nIf you continue to rework or release other content in this direction, I’m seriously considering quitting the game altogether.\n\nThis is a mobile game, not a console or PC game. How much of our time do you actually expect us to dedicate to this game? Do you seriously expect us to spend all day playing it?\n\nPlease, get a grip.", "timestamp": "2026-09-03T00:25:48.370000+00:00", "thread_id": "1544152565921611837", "reactions": [{"emoji": "Celeste_agree", "emoji_id": "1400771815076528258", "count": 14}, {"emoji": "⬆️", "emoji_id": null, "count": 8}], "attachments": [{"id": "1544865964842160229", "filename": "morimens.jpg", "content_type": "image/jpeg", "size": 172869, "url": "https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1544152565921611837/1544865964842160229/morimens.jpg?ex=6a9a100c&is=6a98be8c&hm=4fee3d289b567b5abe99c7e1a7b2cf0501598723639bc3d9699c79d1193187b3&"}, {"id": "1544865965093687316", "filename": "morimens2.jpg", "content_type": "image/jpeg", "size": 539164, "url": "https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1544152565921611837/1544865965093687316/morimens2.jpg?ex=6a9a100c&is=6a98be8c&hm=65f509614fe61e8957c67cd3eacb79cc937c99939a5847f1644d4b078d45d0d5&"}], "thread_title": "D-tide Feedback (New)", "forum_channel_id": "1180845276823564288", "thread_tags": ["1542484945447026708", "1542479601241030726"]}
